{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/806842-moonsilver-artifacts","id":806842,"title":"Moonsilver Artifacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-12T01:02:22-08:00","id":806842,"title":"Moonsilver Artifacts","content":"\u200b&quot;Moonsilver\u2019s Essence is protean and wild. Its Evocations often unite wielder and weapon in a bridge of primal instinct or mystical insight. Its attacks are often either flamboyant and barely-restrained, or else subtle and insidious, laced with poisons, slivers of heart-seeking metal, or ever-bleeding wounds. Some moonsilver Evocations produce physical manifestations in the weapon\u2014while it\u2019s unusual for a moonsilver artifact to flow and reshape itself like water or clay, a longfang might flex to strike around interposing blades, a daiklave might stretch to drive its point deeper into vital organs, and a grimcleaver might release its mighty ax-head to fly into the Lunar\u2019s foes like a moth, only to draw it back in the next moment.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Here are some of my ideas, only a few of which are originally my own. Would you like to share more?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ma-Ha-Suchi's Corpse Drill (3-dot)</b><br /> While this moonsilver direlance seems normal at rest, a decisive attack allows it to reveal its first Evocation, whereby the spearhead twists into a drill and twists further to bore that drill into whomever or whatever it strikes, burying the head deep and fast such that it cannot easily be pulled free. In this weapon's youth, this lead to many a situation that granted it the nickname of &quot;Corpse Hammer&quot;.<br /> <br /> Further Evocations enable the spear's master to free the weapon's blade with a counterspin, or to messily tear its way free with an even more vigorous twist, as well as a method to spin constantly in readiness for any &quot;clean&quot; hit.<br /> <br /> In more carefree days, Ma-Ha-Suchi was once known to use the weapon for particularly violent pole-dances in battle, stabbing straight down into the floor and allowing the weapon to spin him about that he might strike all of those who surrounded him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Sage's Tower (N/A)</b><br /> A sorcerous phylactery in the form of a staff which can alter its length and girth, becoming a half-staff, a quarterstaff, a wrackstaff, or a weapon fit for a warstrider. Once per day, it may assume its greatest size, revealing itself to be a tower in which many can find shelter. This tower is itself one-half of a Lunar-aspected manse. When united with the manse's immobile foundation, the tower-manse's full powers as a place of protection and sorcerous might are realized, though the foundation continues to feed the staff even when the two are separated, no matter how far apart.<br /> <br /> Questionable legends suggest that there are, in fact, six or more additional foundations in the world, in the other Directions of Creation and hidden in stranger worlds. Are they asleep, torn asunder by enemies, or perhaps broken as the cost of invoking some great power laying dormant within the tower-staff? Would more than one lend that much more power to the artifact, or perhaps the staff only drinks of the last foundation with which it was united? Would different foundations give rise to different fortress-towers?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dancing Moon Disk (3-dot)</b><br /> A weapon which is both shield and chakram, the Dancing Moon Disk is an animated and lively weapon which needs not be wielded with the hands. It flies about under its own power, responding to the motions of its master's hands and body, darting and sweeping to strike distant targets and allowing the defense of allies beyond the master's reach. As the master's dance becomes more dominant, the weapon becomes more dramatic and wild.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Flying Silver Dream (3-dot)</b><br /> A cousin to the Dancing Moon Disk, but far more aggressive and to-the-point. A sword without a handle, or perhaps a spear without a haft, the balance of this weapon's weight exchanges the Balanced tag for the Piercing tag, and its Evocations emphasize fast and distant linear thrusts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Shifting Sword (3-dot)</b><br /> Designed by a Lunar swordsman who believed in the virtues of versatility, this weapon is a conventional daiklave at rest, but radically transforms when its master needs the function of a different kind of sword. Altering the distribution of its mass and forsaking Balance, it might become a Chopping blade like a reaver daiklave. For a piercing thrust attack, it reshapes itself into some middleground between a fellsting artifact rapier and the one-handed spear of a longfang. It may grow in size to demand the use of two hands for additional striking power, useful in a Clash, or shrink into a smaller and more dexterous blade when quarters are tight. It may even blunt its edge, becoming much like a tetsubo for a measure of mercy... or perhaps just for the force imparted with a Smashing attack.<br /> <br /> The Shifting Sword obeys a kind of momentum; constantly changing between different forms keeps it flexible and responsive, but consistently using the same transformation will serve to make that transformation easier and more effective, at the cost of rendering it more difficult to achieve any other form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Serpentine Spear (4-dot)</b><br /> Sakura Kyouko's weapon from <i>Puella Magi Madoka Magica</i>. A spear which can segment into seven-section staff, and segment further into a rope-dart where the rope is in fact a weighted chain. Like the Shifting Sword, this weapon emphasizes versatility. Unlike that weapon, the Serpentine Spear trades a metaphorical kind of flexibility for the literal kind, as it must transition through the seven-section staff form when going from one extreme to the other, though mastery of the weapon could make this a lightning-quick affair. Lesser Evocations manipulate the weapon's length, extending the reach and power of strikes or crushing those bound within its coiling chain.<br /> <br /> This weapon might have an Evocation where a successful clinch allows it to transform into a snake familiar made of moonsilver, continuing to constrict and &quot;bite&quot; its victim while the master makes use of her free hands for other tasks. As soon as the clinch fails, the weapon would streak back to its master as quickly as possible, becoming an inanimate weapon once returned to her hands.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Cruel Hunter (3- or 4-dot)</b><br /> Designed by a headstrong, obsessive, and thoroughly unpleasant Lunar who vowed that no prey would escape death at his blade, this reaver daiklave may shatter off a jagged piece of itself should it successfully wound a target. This shard is delivered into the wound, where it will slowly begin to dig and worm and burrow its way through the victim's body. Even should the prey flee, within a day's time the shard may yet slice away the last of the victim's life from within; without a surgeon capable of removing the shard, it will eventually carve its way to his heart and kill him. More than one shard may afflict someone in this way, slim as may be their chances of surviving multiple wounding blows in the first place.<br /> <br /> At its core, this is a patient but tunnel-visioned weapon which trades immediately lethality against any target against assured mortality for a few. Each shard broken away reduces the blade's mass and leaves it less capable of inflicting damage against any victim... at least without an Evocation representing the master's knack for breaking off pieces in a deliberate, serrated pattern that allows the blade to tear viciously with what weight it retains.<br /> <br /> But the weapon's patience is limited indeed, for it harbors its own bloodthirst and despises being diminished. Its master may explore this frustration, coaxing the weapon to hunt for its pieces and their mutual prey, assisting actions to track and locate the victim, and drawing the weapon's blows unerringly past the victim's defenses and into the flesh which traps its shards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Gorgon Aegis (3- or 4-dot)</b><br /> This shield bears the visage of a hideous, snarling woman with snakes for hair. When attuned, this monstrosity comes to life, biting at weapons that strike it to capture them in its teeth and biting at flesh when the shield is smashed against foes. Further Evocations allow the snakes to reach out and strike at more distant targets, as well as lending poison to their fangs. The most dramatic power of this shield is when the Gorgon herself tears free from the shield to join the battle herself, ripping her foes apart with metal claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-20-2017, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T01:42:54-08:00","id":806848,"title":"","content":"Well, I had one idea for a daiklave used by my Eclipse Pirate...<br /> <br /> <b>Sharkbite</b><br /> A Wavecrasher Daiklave (Probably similar in tags to a Reaver Daiklave), this weapon is often surprisingly static for a Moonsilver weapon. That is, until the blade first tastes blood. Then the protean hunting Essence within the Moonsiver begins to awaken. Sharkbite can, with lethal blows, shape itself into a more jagged edge with which to inflict more pain and more easily draw the blood of its prey. If the Daiklave senses blood it has tasted before, it hungers for more and twists mid-strike to help guide its user. For its ultimate Evocation, the blade actually splits down the middle, twisting into an approximation of a wicked beast's jaws to sink its fangs into its prety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:03:40-08:00","id":808750,"title":"","content":"<b>The Maddening Bow (3-dots)</b><br /> <br /> Successful Decisive attacks with Archery tend to leave arrows stuck in people, and people tend to find this stressful. The Maddening Bow magnifies this stress, driving its victims insane with pain, fear, and anger. The wise Lunar uses this Evocation at a healthy distance, because the victim will go berserk and attack the closest target, foe or friend. Assuming they don't simply retreat immediately in a blind panic.<br /> <br /> The next Evocation allows the Lunar to provoke exaggerated reactions with successful Withering attacks; even though the target doesn't suffer a scratch, she is made painfully aware of her brush with death and the next shot may be her end. Again, the Lunar may have very little control over whether the victim responds with fear or rage, though the effects are less pronounced than with the Decisive attack.<br /> <br /> A further Evocation might allow the Lunar to decide which reaction occurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-19-2017, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T10:54:19-08:00","id":808842,"title":"","content":"I've had this idea for a little while but haven't fleshed out all I want it to be yet.<br /> <br /> The Sand-Dancer's Silk<br /> <br /> A shawl made of threaded moonsilver and white jade, it was often used by exalted performers and practitioners of Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style. When used in combination with dances and other visual performances, it's evocations create hypnotizing effects that instill primal emotions and intimacies in those audience members who witness them, such as lust, hunger, fear, anger, or grief. <br /> <br /> It's greatest evocations can even shift the appearance of the wearer as the shawl seems to stretch and completely surround the user, adding additonal appearance dice or allowing social actions to be taken against targets the Exalt may not ordinarily be able to affect, creating a camouflage of shifting colors and textures across the surface, giving the exalt chameleon like stealth capabilities. <br /> <br /> The final evocation acts as a kind of terrifying war form which gives a small penalty to the resolve of enemies and a small bonus to the use of improvised weapons (a la Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Style) and bare handed attacks as the shawl surround the Exalt and shifts into a terrifying form and absorbs improvised weapons to be used and switched between freely as they shift within this form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T11:48:34-08:00","id":808904,"title":"","content":"Written for one of my players in an upcoming game:<br /> <br /> <b>Seshetamun</b><br /> Known variously as the <i>Lance of Celestial Order</i> and the <i>Quill that Marks the Wicked in the Book of the Dead, </i>this moonsilver dire lance is a weapon of fair but inexorable vengeance. When attuned by a Lunar wielder it may be banished into a shaft of moonlight, where it waits until its owner draws it forth from Luna's radiance again. Its Evocations can draw in the blood of an enemy to read the secret sins of their hearts, turning that blood to poisonous ink and scribing a curse that saps the enemy's strength and hastens his demise. It can be hurled in a flash of silvery light to impale a fleeing enemy's shadow, transfixing him so that Seshetamun's wielder can bring vengeance to bear. The final Evocation exacts a painful price upon one whom the wielder has declared her enemy and brought to bay, maiming him in proportion to the crimes he has committed before quieting again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Share your wonders in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop#post823884\" target=\"_blank\">The Artifact and Evocation Workshop</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1315-ferryman","name":"Ferryman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1315_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T01:08:42-08:00","id":810135,"title":"","content":"<b>The Silver Harrier</b><br /> Named both for the species of hawk and the tactic of harrying prey, this moonsilver bow is characterized by patience, preparation, and its power to animate the arrows it fires.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first Evocation can only be used against non-trivial opponents -- those whom the archer knows have the skill to avoid the shot at all; a trivial opponent could be struck dead without the need for such strategy. Against real opponents, this Evocation is a special Withering attack that resets the archer to base Initiative as though it were Decisive. All of the Initiative the archer loses is conferred to the arrow, along with any Initiative it steals from the target.<br /> <br /> After the arrow flies past its target, it circles around to attack the same target again in the next round, with its turn determined by its Initiative score.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the master of the bow will be able to fire hunting arrows that remain in flight indefinitely, capable of performing their own Withering attacks to continue building their Initiative, and capable of Decisive attacks that finally end their flights, whether to score lethal injury or to perform Gambits (such as Disarming the target, or Distracting them to lend that collected Initiative to another Decisive attack from the bow's master or one of his allies).<br /> <br /> Other advanced tricks would include the ability to fire arrows directly into the air to circle overhead without a specific target, even before a battle begins -- the bow's master uses an Evocation akin to Naked Fang Draw (Steel Devil Style) to lend some of the Initiative generated by his Join Battle results with these prepared arrows. He may also call them all down at once as part of the special Rain of Feathered Death attack Evocation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T10:29:09-08:00","id":810278,"title":"","content":"<b>The Singing Sword</b><br /> <br /> When unsheathed, the blade of this moonsilver daiklave constantly vibrates, humming a song to itself and anyone who may be listening. It may be used as a musical instrument with Performance actions where the swordsman produces notes by swinging and slicing at air, or by striking stone or metal objects. The musical swordsman may flurry such Performance actions with attacks and object-destroying feats of strength, without penalty.<br /> <br /> Even though attacks and parrying defenses with the Singing Sword are always made with the musical swordsman's Melee Ability score, the weapon has a special interaction with the Charms of Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style. Attacks with the Singing Sword count as Kiai attacks made with Voice of the Night Bird for the purposes of the Style's other Charms. These attacks do <b>not</b> receive the raw damage bonus provided by Nightingale's Form Charm.<br /> <br /> Further Evocations are possible for a Nightingale Stylist who sings duets with her musical instrument.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I had the idea that the Nightingale Form Charm could provide a +1 Parry bonus for the Singing Sword on top of its other benefits for the martial artist, and that the sword would let you use its Parry Defense with Hearing the Heart's Song and Harmony In Opposition Stance, but that seemed inconsistent with denying the sword's attacks the Form Charm's raw damage bonus.<br /> <br /> Rather, the musical swordsman's Performance score could be used to enhance the use of the Sword through the Sword's own Evocations, or else you just need more than the initial Evocation in order to synergize the weapon with the Style's Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Singing Sword is another weapon which could have an associated manse -- some kind of massive musical facility which sings in harmony with the sword. However, this manse would be very hard to hide, and a duet where one partner is too far way for the audience to hear is kind of silly. So the idea needs refinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T11:55:24-08:00","id":810313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/806842-moonsilver-artifacts#post806842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Ma-Ha-Suchi's Corpse Driller</b></div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Is uh... Is that what he's calling it these days?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'm so sorry)</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T21:07:13-08:00","id":810482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/806842-moonsilver-artifacts?p=810313#post810313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'm so sorry)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Not sorry enough, apparently.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Tricky Spider (4-dots)</b><br /> <br /> A moonsilver artifact yo-yo, this weapon's string may extend to prodigious lengths and its striking head may unfold into a spider. This allows it to grab objects and function as a grappling hook, disarm or retrieve weapons, or latch onto enemies. When grasping an enemy, the spider may deliver venomous bites or else scurry all over their body to wind its extending string about them, restricting their limbs. Alternatively, the weapon's master may transfer his conscious into the spider, two bodies connected by the moonsilver thread between them; in this way, the master can infiltrate blocked areas through tiny openings, unlocking doors or spying out useful information.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> The yoyo has a single Hearthstone socket. The end of the string is not tied around a finger, but affixed to a moonsilver ring. When not in use, the yoyo can shrink and attach itself to the ring as a spider signet, with any Hearthstone likewise shrinking to become a tiny jewel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-19-2017, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T12:04:54-08:00","id":810721,"title":"","content":"<b>Argent Coat (based on Busou Renkin's <a href=\"http://busorenkin.wikia.com/wiki/Silver_Skin\" target=\"_blank\">Silver Skin</a>) (Light artifact armor; Buoyant, Silent)</b><br /> <br /> An artifact buff jacket made from the hide of a beast with remarkable regenerative healing, cured in liquid moonsilver, and woven with moonsilver threads, the Silver Skin covers the user's entire body but is extremely lightweight and flexible, posing only enough restriction to movement that it impedes the use Martial Arts which forbid any form of armor.<br /> <br /> The Evocations of this armor harden the material in response to strikes, offering additional Soak against Withering attacks and Hardness against Decisive attacks. However, even when its Evocations are fully mastered, this defense is torn apart with every attack and does not fully repair itself until the wearer's next turn -- repeated strikes will tear the defense away to nothing, leaving the armor's master vulnerable. Too, these Evocations offer less protection against attacks that would cause bashing damage than lethal or aggravated.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Silver Shell (Heavy artifact armor)</b><br /> <br /> An artifact suit of articulated plate armor. Its first Evocation removes its mobility penalty and grants it the Buoyant and Silent tags. Further Evocations not only mimic the protections of the Silver Skin, but also allow the armor to produce natural weaponry and additional limbs through shapeshifting its own substance. These are modeled by the Supernatural Merits: claws, horns, quills, even tails, wings, extra arms, and quicksilver venom.<br /> <br /> With a slaved and dedicated manse to provide extra power (and material), this armor could even transform into a warstrider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-06-2017, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:29:02-08:00","id":810843,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for an artifact, though I've never been sure how to implement it. How would one create a living artifact weapon? Though I suppose it could be mechanical rather than actually alive.<br /> <br /> <b>The Hive Mind</b><br /> <br /> Rather than actually being composed of moonsilver, the scabbard seems to be composed of the same material as bee hives. Once the owner reaches their hand into the overly large scabbard hole, they are able to unsheathe sword-shaped moonsilver automatons that look suspiciously insectoid. Evocations allow the wielder to bring them to life and attack on their own. Legend tells of a technique that summons the queen-mother of this hive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/899-the-free-man","name":"The Free Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar899_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T15:50:32-08:00","id":810852,"title":"","content":"<b>The Puppeteer's Blade</b><br /> <br /> This moonsilver knife is easily concealable, supernaturally so, and ready to draw with the quickest of movements. Its evocations can infect a target with quicksilver essence with even the slightest of cuts, deadening limbs and paralyzing the body. It even allows the wielder to seize those threads of essence and conduct the victim, much like a marionette on strings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T14:35:00-07:00","id":866527,"title":"","content":"As mentioned in the Vault sub-category of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/866523-moon-base\">moon-based, Lunar-aspected supply manses</a>, there could be a moonsilver artifact weapon that creates copies of any creature it is used to kill.<br /> <br /> These copies sleep in the vault manse until summoned, which might only be possible on moonlit nights, especially if the copies are crafted from moonlight.<br /> <br /> In this way, a Solar can touch a bit more upon the experience of Lunar hunting, or a Lunar can gain servants as well as Heart's Blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:31:52-07:00","id":866545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Free Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/806842-moonsilver-artifacts?p=810313#post810313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> Is uh... Is that what he's calling it these days?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">(I'm so sorry)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually Corpse Drill, not Driller. It might make a bit of difference, it might not...<br /> <br /> <b>Invasion</b><br /> <br /> Incursio from Akame ga Kill. All of this tends to come rather further into the series, so spoiler tags ahoy!<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Made from a powerful &quot;dangerous beast&quot;, it's basically a Juggernaut in a suit, supposing that the wearer can answer its potential. Lower level Evocations involve adaptive camouflage invisibility like in Predator, as well as furnishing the wearer with weaponry (its normal form is actually that of a daiklave instead of a suit of armor, so one could argue that the most basic Evocation is turning it into the armor). Higher-level Evocations allow it to take on new environments and movement forms. It doesn't dissuade the recklessly selfless from taking the Prometheus school of running away from or otherwise avoiding large falling objects, though.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T15:43:31-07:00","id":866548,"title":"","content":"Luna's Blood- Apparently just a mass of liquid moonsilver, attuning to this Artifact requires the would-be user drain their veins of all blood and let the Artifact fill the gap. In exchange for the risk of death if they ever cancel attunement, this Artifact grants immense skill, allowing the user to fill the gaps of missing flesh with the liquid to heal wounds and create armor, or to shape the spilt liquid into tools, weapons, or even minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T16:13:08-07:00","id":872705,"title":"","content":"Inspired by the dragonslayer and onislayer bows and arrows of <i>Dark Souls</i>...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>GIANT SLAYER (Medium Artifact, Moonsilver Powerbow)</b><br /> <br /> The first Evocation of this weapon might become available automatically, or else the bow demands that the master first use it to fire the killing shot against a creature larger than the master, or at least as large as a bull moose. The Evocation allows the master to summon enormous arrows (practically javelins) made purely of moonsilver. The mass of these missiles inflicts greater damage than mundane arrows, but they require great strength to fire at all, let alone accurately, and they lose one range band of effective range. These arrows will disappear when the moon next sets from the sky, though they can also be banished with the master's touch.<br /> <br /> The second Evocation draws power from the moon. The brighter the moon shines in the sky, the brighter the bow and moonsilver arrows shine in turn. This makes using the moonsilver arrows easier.<br /> <br /> The third Evocation summons more moonsilver arrows around one which is already in flight, turning a single shot into a hailstorm of magical silver death. This attack can only be used a limited number of times before the present arrows must be retrieved and banished back to their resting place.<br /> <br /> The fourth Evocation requires the master to fire an arrow of any kind straight at the moon in the sky. If his heart and aim are true, the Lunar-aspected manse on the moon responds to the prayer of the bow's master, and fires down a single moonsilver arrow the size of a tree. This is an unblockable attack which is likewise undodgeable by any creature with the Legendary Size merit. This attack almost always causes massive damage to the ground beneath the target's feet.<br /> <br /> There might be a fifth Evocation which makes the moonsilver arrows better at piercing the hides of giant creatures, or else which causes the arrows to dig and burrow inside, cutting and tearing ever-deeper wounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T21:28:11-07:00","id":876255,"title":"","content":"<b>KEROBEROS, THE THREE-HEADED HOUND (3-dot, Medium Artifact, Moonsilver)</b><br /> <i>Tags: Bashing, Lethal, Melee, Reaching, Smashing, Piercing, Chopping, Two-Handed</i><br /> <br /> A polearm with a three-ended head. It features a hammer on one end and an axe-blade on the other, with a spear tip at the top. Each of the business ends is embossed with the profile of a snarling hound's head on both sides.<br /> <br /> This weapon's first three Evocations reshape the head, concentrating all mass into the hammer, axe, or spear for a superior version of a Smashing, Chopping, or Piercing attack, respectively.<br /> <br /> The fourth Evocation splits the weapon into three smaller weapons, each featuring just one of the heads. All three belong to the Light weight-class, may be wielded with just one hand, and Thrown.<br /> <br /> The fifth Evocation allows the master to recall any of the three individual weapons from across any distance, as long as he still holds or carries at least one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-19-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T09:22:07-07:00","id":881892,"title":"","content":"<b>THE WATCHDOG SHIELD (Medium)</b><br /> <br /> The face of this moonsilver shield is molded into the face of a noble, vigilantly-staring hound, with polished moonstones for its unblinking eyes, around which its Evocations are focused. Any Solar or Lunar who attunes to the shield can use its eyes to see when their own are blinded; the Watchdog's Eyes may see even in utter darkness as the gems begin to glow.<br /> <br /> The Watchdog's Eyes alert the master to unseen dangers. By mastering the Shield's Evocations, it will keep watch at all times for ambushes and unexpected attacks, up to and including those from invisible sources. If held at the ready before a fight begins, it enhances the master's Join Battle. It knows who the enemy intends to attack, and how, as soon as the enemy himself does, assisting the master's ability to parry or clash attacks against himself or anyone whom he is protecting with a Defend Other action. It likewise warns when the enemy intends to advance or retreat, assisting the master's ability to thwart his foe's Rush and Disengage actions. It might also counter or hinder the effectiveness of Distraction gambits against its master, and pierce illusions that would prevent her from properly defending herself.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-04-2016, 12:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T00:49:04-07:00","id":882646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/806842-moonsilver-artifacts?p=810721#post810721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"http://busorenkin.wikia.com/wiki/Silver_Skin\" target=\"_blank\">Silver Skin</a> (Light artifact armor; Buoyant, Silent)</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Silverskin is the canonical name of Raksi's armour and the notion of her dressing like that amuses me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T22:50:42-07:00","id":901778,"title":"","content":"<b>DEADLY TRACERS (Light)</b><br /> <br /> A pair of short daiklaves, orichalcum and moonsilver, made to be wielded by an assassin striking from the shadows. They can both be attuned by a Solar or Lunar Exalt.<br /> <br /> The orichalcum sword, Gold Tracer, gains its name from the streaks of golden light the blade trails behind. When fighting in darkness, an experienced wielder can weave these flashes together in a pattern that mesmerizes opponents and lowers their guard.<br /> <br /> The moonsilver sword, Silver Tracer, gains its name from the toxic quicksilver it delivers into the victim's bloodstream, streaking its way throughout the entire body from a single wound.<br /> <br /> Both blades are adept at tracing the major veins and arteries of their victim's, opening up greatly bleeding wounds. Blood-loss makes lightheaded victims more susceptible to Gold Tracer's distracting light, and emptier veins give the deadly quicksilver easier passage through the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:09:35-07:00","id":1070176,"title":"","content":"<b>BEASTHOOD COWL</b><br /> <br /> A hooded cloak made with the hide of a beast, threaded and decorated with moonsilver, and sometimes another material that resonates with the essence of the slain creature. Donning this cowl allows the wearer to evoke the strength and powers of the beast, even to the extent of assuming its form.<br /> <br /> Such an artifact allows the wearer to step into the experience of being a Lunar Exalt, but their lack of resonance with moonsilver means that they display a Tell which can give their identity away to those who know their true face, and they may partially lose their minds as long as they remain transformed, with a risk of going insane with prolonged or repeated use.<br /> <br /> Lunar and Solar Exalted, being more resonant with moonsilver than anyone else, have no Tells at all when using the cowl to transform, and risk no loss of identity or control.<br /> <br /> Aside from hiding their Tells, the benefit of the cowl for Lunar Exalted is being able to add the strength of the slain creature to whichever form they currently wear underneath, and also to access a different War Form than their own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:49:23-08:00","id":1165747,"title":"","content":"<b>Silverskin</b> (the idea above has been renamed to Argent Coat, so that both are more accurate)<br /> <br /> An idea which seems much more characteristic of Rakshi, the vain Queen of Fangs.<br /> <br /> This moonsilver Silken Armor infuses itself into the wearer, leaving them naked if they weren't wearing anything else. Their skin turns silver; they look like Marvel's Silver Surfer.<br /> <br /> In this state, the armor gives the wearer the Chameleon Merit, with the same bonus for being naked. If the wearer has the Chameleon Merit, then they get another bonus die. They can also change their color to look like natural skin, and thus hide the possibility that they're &quot;wearing&quot; any armor at all.<br /> <br /> This armor's Evocations assist with healing from injuries (or perhaps simply having ablative extra -0 health levels that regenerate in combat time) and also camouflaging stealth effects, which gives Solar Resistance (possibly also Medicine) and Solar Stealth some potentials to boost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Plumage of the Lunar Peacock</b><br /> <br /> Not artifact armor at all, except when enhanced by the appropriate Dreaming Pearl Courtesan Charm.<br /> <br /> This moonsilver-threaded silk robe can shapeshift into any set of clothing, greatly assisting the wearer in disguise rolls and synergizing with Solar Larceny-based disguise and persona Charms, as well as possibly also Socialize-based persona Charms. The clothes resist wear, tear, and soiling, and assist with keeping the wearer clean and presentable; together with enabling the wearer to always be best-dressed for any occasion, the wearer can avoid most appearance-based penalties, and perhaps enjoy some benefits to social influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T18:38:03-08:00","id":1167813,"title":"","content":"<b>Subtle Glove</b><br /> <br /> A leather glove made from moonsilver and the hide of a venomous chameleon creature. The glove will fit any hand, paw, claw, tentacle, or similar appendage, and adjust to match changes in that appendage.<br /> <br /> When attuned, the glove changes to match the appearance of that appendage entirely, except for a Tell. This Tell works exactly like a Lunar Tell; only those who have seen the glove's true form have the opportunity to notice its presence on the assassin's hand.<br /> <br /> With a touch and an expenditure of Essence, the glove channels a contact poison into the victim's skin, briefly revealing itself in the process. The assassin can use the same effect to poison blades, needles, food, or water. More poison is delivered through damage, and the glove can deliver poison directly through a damaging attack when the appendage underneath is capable of making lacerating or puncturing attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T18:52:20-08:00","id":1167814,"title":"","content":"<b>FLESH IS WEAK (Articulated Plate, rating 5)</b><br /> <br /> A suit of articulated plate which hastens efforts to put it on and take it off, that it may quickly rescue its master from the vulnerabilities of flesh, and swiftly release him unto its pleasures.<br /> <br /> Once fully suited, the wearer can use a miscellaneous action to fuse with the armor while transforming the flesh and bones of his organic body into the living metal chassis of a moonsilver golem with stats superior to mere articular plate, and without a Mobility penalty.<br /> <br /> He's still super-heavy and cannot swim, but he can attack and parry as though his body was a light artifact weapon.<br /> <br /> He becomes immune to suffocation, poison, disease, burning heat and freezing cold, but he will suffer deprivation from thirst and hunger. His bite attack becomes a heavy artifact weapon, but nothing he swallows will satisfy his thirst or hunger.<br /> <br /> Not only is this transformed state compatible with Incomparable Body Armor, casting that spell can substitute for the miscellaneous transformation action.<br /> <br /> The transformed state synergizes well with Athletics Charms for feats of strength and Resistance Charms for armor-enhancement and damage-resistance.<br /> <br /> <br /> It could also allow the return of <b>Weapon-Trapping Body Dominion</b>, that <i>extremely </i>Liminal-esque Second Edition Charm where the Lunar could trap a weapon in her body after being stabbed with it. Though that fits less with &quot;Maximum Hardness!&quot; and more with T-1000 &quot;I heal any damage you inflict on me&quot;.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-15-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T07:17:24-08:00","id":1168184,"title":"","content":"<b>Stolen Behemoth Heart (Hearthstone 4 or Artifact \u00a7</b> <b>5)<br /> <br /> [<i>Evangelion</i> S2 Engine]</b><br /> <br /> First Age Artifice is allowed to do things which artifacts cannot normally be allowed to do, for fear of breaking the setting.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it is allowed to produce artifacts which function like hearthstones; especially if that is <i>all</i> they do.<br /> <br /> The Stolen Behemoth Heart could be just a hearthstone, or it could be a First Age Artifact of the same rough size as the average Hearthstone. Either way, when you plug it into a warstrider, you not only provide the machine with fuel, you super-charge the metal monster to the point of reducing its attunement cost.<br /> <br /> For Lunar Exalted, it would have the alternative function of reducing the cost of Towering Beast Shape and similar Charms for assuming forms of Legendary Size.<br /> <br /> As an artifact, it would lack a hearthstone's dependence on a manse, and thus avoid a lot of vulnerability and restricted range that comes with most manses.<br /> <br /> Of course, one of the components for making it would be the undying heart of a slain behemoth from beyond Creation.<br /> <br /> And it goes without saying that plugging this monstrous wonder into the Walking Devil Tower is probably an <i>apocalyptically</i> bad idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T18:32:04-08:00","id":1168452,"title":"","content":"<b>The Hungry Knife</b><br /> <br /> When this dagger delivers a killing blow or stabs into the corpse of a person slain by its wielder, the blade consume the corpse utterly. The blade can likewise be used to absorb bloodstains created by a preceding struggle.<br /> <br /> For a Lunar Exalt, the knife will produce a single drop of blood from its pommel by which Luna's Chosen can gain the victim's Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> An Evocation allows for the knife to clothe the assassin in the victim's clothing while storing any of the Lunar's own clothing within a special dimensional pocket.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}